## Workflow Guidelines

### 1. Making Changes

```bash
# Create a new branch
git checkout -b {{branchPattern | default 'feature'}}/your-feature

# Make changes and test
npm test

# Commit with descriptive message
git commit -m "feat: add new feature"

# Push and open PR
git push origin {{branchPattern | default 'feature'}}/your-feature
```

### 2. Before Committing

```bash
# Verify tests pass
npm test

# Check code quality
npm run lint:all

# Review changes
git diff
git status
```

## Commit Message Format

Follow conventional commits:

```
type(scope): description

body (optional)

footer (optional)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

Types:
- `feat:` — New feature
- `fix:` — Bug fix
- `docs:` — Documentation only
- `test:` — Test changes
- `refactor:` — Code refactoring
- `chore:` — Maintenance

Example:

```
feat({{skillSlug}}): add new functionality

Adds comprehensive new feature with validation.
Includes unit and integration tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

## Troubleshooting

### Skill Not Showing in Claude Code

```bash
# Verify skill is in correct location
ls ~/.claude/skills/{{skillSlug}}/

{{#hasSkillDirectory}}
# Verify structure
ls skill/SKILL.md{{#hasPluginDirectory}} plugin/manifest.json{{/hasPluginDirectory}}

{{/hasSkillDirectory}}
# Restart Claude Code
# Settings → Skills → Refresh
```

### Tests Failing

```bash
# Run with verbose output
npm test -- --verbose

# Check specific test file
npm test -- name-of-test.test.js

# See test output without coverage
npm test -- --no-coverage
```

